    termsParagraph2: '<p class="muted">Using this site\'s practice questions or mock exams does not satisfy the New York State Motorcycle Safety Program (NYSMSP) Basic RiderCourse (BRC) or Basic RiderCourse 2 License/Waiver (BRC2-LW) requirement -- completing an approved course waives only the DMV road/skills test, never the Class M written knowledge test, which every applicant must still pass with at least 14 of 20 questions correct, including at least 2 of the 4 road-sign questions. Our content is a supplementary study aid only, and does not issue any official course-completion certificate. Completing practice exams here also does not register you for, or schedule, the official DMV written knowledge test or an NYSMSP course; official testing is administered by the New York State DMV, and rider training is administered by NYSMSP-affiliated sites. While we strive to align our content with the current New York State DMV Motorcycle Manual, it is provided "as-is" for self-study and does not constitute legal or driving-instruction advice or a guaranteed exam outcome.</p>',
