    termsParagraph2: "<p class=\"muted\">Using this site's practice questions does not fulfill any Washington notary requirement and does not register you with, or issue any credential from, the Washington State Department of Licensing (DOL) — our content is a supplementary study aid only. Washington does not require notary applicants to complete a training course or pass an exam: under RCW 42.45.200, an applicant must simply be at least 18 years old, be a Washington resident or have a place of employment or practice in the state, be able to read and write English, execute an oath of office, and submit a surety bond in the amount and form set by DOL rule before the director issues a four-year commission. Completing practice questions here does not submit an application, post a bond, execute an oath, or schedule any part of that process, which is handled directly by DOL. While we strive to align our content with the current Washington Revised Code Chapter 42.45 (the Uniform Law on Notarial Acts), it is provided \"as-is\" for self-study and does not constitute legal advice or a guaranteed outcome.</p>",
